{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":1,"id":"next-js","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next.js"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Kirana works with both of Next.js's bundlers: "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turbopack"}]},{"type":"text","value":", the default for\ndevelopment and production builds, and webpack ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--webpack</span>","source":"--webpack"}},{"type":"text","value":"). Server components work\nunchanged. Tested on every change by "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"examples/next-turbopack","source":"examples/next-turbopack"}},{"type":"text","value":" and\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"examples/next-webpack","source":"examples/next-webpack"}},{"type":"text","value":", with npm and pnpm, in a production build and on the dev\nserver."}]},{"type":"component","name":"npm-status","attributes":{},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-fast-way","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The fast way"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"In the project's root:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"npx kirana-style@latest init","lang":"bash","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-prompt\">$</span> <span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style@latest init","variant":"terminal"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It detects Next.js and its bundler, shows every change below as a diff, writes\nthem once you say yes, and prints the install command ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--install</span>","source":"--install"}},{"type":"text","value":" runs it). Then\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-command\">npx</span> kirana-style doctor","source":"npx kirana-style doctor"}},{"type":"text","value":" checks the result. The steps it takes are the ones this page\nshows, so you can also do them by hand."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-install","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install"}]},{"type":"component","name":"install","attributes":{"packages":"@kirana-style/core","dev":"@kirana-style/next @kirana-style/postcss postcss"},"children":[]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-wrap-the-configuration","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Wrap the configuration"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import type { NextConfig } from \"next\"\nimport { withKirana } from \"@kirana-style/next\"\n\nconst nextConfig: NextConfig = {\n  // your Next.js configuration\n}\n\nexport default withKirana(nextConfig)","lang":"ts","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">type</span> { <span class=\"th-token th-type\">NextConfig</span> } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;next&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> { withKirana } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/next&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> nextConfig: <span class=\"th-token th-type\">NextConfig</span> = {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// your Next.js configuration</span>\n}\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">default</span> <span class=\"th-token th-function\">withKirana</span>(nextConfig)","file":"next.config.ts","title":"next.config.ts"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"withKirana","source":"withKirana"}},{"type":"text","value":" configures both bundlers: a Turbopack rule that compiles your\nscripts, and the webpack plugin for "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"next build --webpack","source":"next build --webpack"}},{"type":"text","value":". Rules you already have\nfor the same files are kept."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-add-the-postcss-plugin","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Add the PostCSS plugin"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"export default {\n  plugins: {\n    \"@kirana-style/postcss\": {},\n    // Tailwind CSS, autoprefixer and the rest stay as they are.\n  },\n}","lang":"js","html":"export default {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">plugins</span>: {\n    &quot;@kirana-style/postcss&quot;: {},\n    // Tailwind CSS, autoprefixer and the rest stay as they are.\n  },\n}","file":"postcss.config.mjs","title":"postcss.config.mjs"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-put-the-stylesheet-in-your-global-css","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Put the stylesheet in your global CSS"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"@kirana;","lang":"css","html":"@kirana;","file":"app/globals.css","title":"app/globals.css"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The root layout already imports "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"globals.css","source":"globals.css"}},{"type":"text","value":". The PostCSS plugin replaces\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">@kirana</span>;","source":"@kirana;"}},{"type":"text","value":" with the whole stylesheet: one file, every atom once."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-type-sx","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Type "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sx"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"/// <reference types=\"@kirana-style/core/react\" />","lang":"ts","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-comment\">/// &lt;reference types=&quot;@kirana-style/core/react&quot; /&gt;</span>","file":"kirana.d.ts","title":"kirana.d.ts"}},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"6-write-a-component","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6. Write a component"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import { css } from \"@kirana-style/core\"\n\nconst styles = {\n  title: css({ fontSize: \"2rem\", color: { base: \"#111\", \":hover\": \"#555\" } }),\n}\n\nexport default function Page() {\n  return <h1 sx={styles.title}>Hello</h1>\n}","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> { css } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/core&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">const</span> styles = {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-property\">title</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">fontSize</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;2rem&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-property\">color</span>: { <span class=\"th-token th-property\">base</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;#111&quot;</span>, <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;:hover&quot;</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;#555&quot;</span> } }),\n}\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">default</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"th-token th-function\">Page</span>() {\n  <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">return</span> &lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">h1</span> <span class=\"th-token th-attr\">sx</span>={styles.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">title</span>}&gt;Hello&lt;/<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">h1</span>&gt;\n}","file":"app/page.tsx","title":"app/page.tsx"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That is a server component: "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"sx","source":"sx"}},{"type":"text","value":" compiles to a class string at build time, so\nnothing of Kirana runs at request time. In your editor, the line shows what the\nelement gets; see "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/tooling/editor","children":[{"type":"text","value":"editor support"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"how-the-stylesheet-gets-built","children":[{"type":"text","value":"How the stylesheet gets built"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Turbopack runs loaders, not bundler plugins, so no single step sees every module.\nKirana splits the work the way Tailwind CSS v4 does: the loader rewrites each\nmodule's styles into class names, and the PostCSS plugin compiles the project into\nthe stylesheet. The two never talk: they agree because a class name is a hash of\nwhat it styles, never of the order modules were built in. In development the\nplugin tells Next.js which folders to watch, so an edit to a component reaches the\npage without a restart."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The cost is measured in the design note\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"packages/kirana/design-notes/turbopack.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">md</span>","source":"packages/kirana/design-notes/turbopack.md"}},{"type":"text","value":": 53 ms to compile the 104 scripts of this documentation site the first time, 5 ms\nafter an edit. One difference from the other adapters: the stylesheet holds the\natoms of every script in the project, imported or not."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"with-webpack-only","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With webpack only"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A project that always builds with "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-attr\">--webpack</span>","source":"--webpack"}},{"type":"text","value":" can skip PostCSS and use the webpack\nadapter on its own:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"install","attributes":{"packages":"@kirana-style/core","dev":"@kirana-style/webpack"},"children":[]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import { withKirana } from \"@kirana-style/webpack/next\"\n\nexport default withKirana({})","lang":"js","html":"import { withKirana } from &quot;@kirana-style/webpack/next&quot;\n\nexport default <span class=\"th-token th-function\">withKirana</span>({})","file":"next.config.js","title":"next.config.js"}},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"source":"import \"@kirana-style/core/stylesheet.css\"","lang":"jsx","html":"import &quot;@kirana-style/core/stylesheet.<span class=\"th-token th-property\">css</span>&quot;","file":"app/layout.jsx","title":"app/layout.jsx"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next runs a server and a client compiler over the same app, and a server\ncomponent is only seen by the server one. Every compiler of a project shares one\ncompiler session, which is how those atoms reach the stylesheet the client writes.\nDetails in "},{"type":"link","href":"/docs/integrations/bundlers#nextjs","children":[{"type":"text","value":"other bundlers"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"With webpack, a style change in "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"next dev --webpack","source":"next dev --webpack"}},{"type":"text","value":" shows after a reload: CSS\nhot updates are not implemented for webpack."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"next","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Next"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"/docs/start/first-component","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your first component"}]},{"type":"text","value":": a button with a hover state\nand a variant, and the CSS it compiles to."}]}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"next-js","text":"Next.js","level":1},{"id":"the-fast-way","text":"The fast way","level":2},{"id":"1-install","text":"1. Install","level":2},{"id":"2-wrap-the-configuration","text":"2. Wrap the configuration","level":2},{"id":"3-add-the-postcss-plugin","text":"3. Add the PostCSS plugin","level":2},{"id":"4-put-the-stylesheet-in-your-global-css","text":"4. Put the stylesheet in your global CSS","level":2},{"id":"5-type-sx","text":"5. Type sx","level":2},{"id":"6-write-a-component","text":"6. Write a component","level":2},{"id":"how-the-stylesheet-gets-built","text":"How the stylesheet gets built","level":2},{"id":"with-webpack-only","text":"With webpack only","level":2},{"id":"next","text":"Next","level":2}]}
